# G055 — Product Inventory

*v2. See `product-inventory.md` for prose: movement log (receive/sell),
derived quantity from sum of movements, restock threshold, category views.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Monthly Stock Audit

[monthly-stock-audit @month-end @monthly-budget
    IN ORDER TO
        verify low-stock products are flagged
        confirm restock budget covers needed purchases
        and report the month's inventory valuation

    @inventory <- [inventory[load {as-of: @month-end}]]
    @needed    <- [inventory[restock-needed]]
    @valuation <- [inventory[total-value]]

    concurrent [
        <- @sarah{verify low-stock skus: @needed:skus}
        <- @kathryn{allocate restock cost against budget: @monthly-budget}
    ]
    join

    where
        every low-stock sku is accounted for
        and kathryn approved the budget allocation
        and valuation is positive
        || -> #audit-open @resistance:reason
]

---

## Verb Surface

[inventory
    new
    add-product      {product}
    receive          {sku, qty}
    sell             {sku, qty}              ;; || insufficient-stock
    quantity         {sku}
    history          {sku}
    total-value
    restock-needed
    by-category      {category}
    load             {as-of}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: quantity as derived from movement log

[inventory[quantity {sku: @sku}
    where
        result equals sum of receives minus sum of sells for @sku
        computed from the append-only movement log
        no separate quantity field to get out of sync
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @inv <- [inventory[new]]
    [inventory[add-product {product: {sku: "WIDGET-A", name: "Widget A",
                                        category: "widgets", price: 499,
                                        restock-threshold: 10}}]]

    [inventory[receive {sku: "WIDGET-A", qty: 50}]]
    [inventory[sell    {sku: "WIDGET-A", qty: 12}]]
    -> [inventory[quantity {sku: "WIDGET-A"}]]     ;; -> 38

    [inventory[sell {sku: "WIDGET-A", qty: 30}]]
    -> [inventory[quantity {sku: "WIDGET-A"}]]     ;; -> 8 (below threshold)
    -> [inventory[restock-needed]]:count            ;; -> 1

    [inventory[sell {sku: "WIDGET-A", qty: 100}]]
        || -> "insufficient-stock"
]
